  "description_text": "Rebuilt in 2026. An entire 1890 row house on South Boston's East Side, taken down to the studs and rebuilt to a current standard - four levels, single-family, no association, no condo fee.The main level runs the full depth of the house around a full-slab quartz waterfall island seating four: custom Lucas cabinetry, Bosch double wall ovens, panel-integrated refrigeration, vein-matched quartz backsplash. The living room opens off it around a floor-to-ceiling quartz gas fireplace set in illuminated white oak built-ins.The entire third floor is the primary suite - three skylights, skyline views, a quartz spa bath with dual rain heads, fitted walk-in closet.Three full baths and a powder room: a bath on every level. Wide-plank white oak throughout, central heat and air.The finished garden level has its own street entrance and full bath.Roof deck with skyline views, private rear deck, off-street parking available . East Broadway, the waterfront and the Seaport minutes away.",
